For the GS-07 Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-05 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following:
1) Inducts, programs, and coordinates special projects, specific and minor work, engineering scopes, studies and designs, and contracts from initial customer request to completion of work and final billing;
2) Assist in planning, coordination of job scheduling, materials, and funding;
3) Provides technical recommendations/solutions to problems;
4) Manages, organizes, and tracks work inducted to PWD; and
5) Works with clients to clarify scope of work, financial obligations, and desired completion dates For the GS-08: Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-07 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following:
1) Inducts, programs, and coordinates special projects, specific and minor work, engineering scopes, studies and designs, and contracts from initial customer request to completion of work and final billing;
2) Works independent in planning, coordination of job scheduling, materials, and funding;
3) Provides technical recommendations/solutions to complex problems;
4) Manages, organizes, and tracks work inducted to PWD; and
5) Works with clients to clarify scope of work, financial obligations, and desired completion dates. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website:
